## Lore

Robo-Gladiators are pilots trained to fight in the Robodome arena, spending more time in the cockpit than most mercenaries. They are showmen as much as warriors: they make their giant robots and power armor look imposing, play to the crowd, toy with slower opponents and finish with a flourish. Outside the arena they are celebrities across Upper Michigan, lower Canada and the Coalition ''Burbs, often confident to the point of arrogance and quick to defend their reputation in a brawl. They are skilled fighters but not soldiers; most know little of military strategy, command or real war.

## GM Notes

**Owned machines:** a Robo-Gladiator typically owns one combat robot or suit of power armor that is his specialty, sometimes a secondary unit as well; the richest Champions own whole garages of them. Most also own a car, ATV, hovercycle or other civilian transport. None of this is in the starting equipment and is applied by hand.

**Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists:** several sets of fashionable civilian clothes, a team outfit, a fire extinguisher, a watch, a duffel bag and travel luggage, and 1D4x10,000 credits'' worth of spare parts.

**Discounts:** active Robodome League gladiators get 40% off Northern Gun products while competing; the current Top Fifty get 60%.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'robo-gladiator');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'robo-gladiator';

